Fall back to the raw host path when resolving an absolute shebang interpreter.

FEX resolves an absolute `#!` interpreter path only as `<rootfs><path>`. On a
non-merged distro rootfs (the FEXRootFSFetcher Fedora image has no `/nix`), a
wrapper whose shebang points at a Nix-store bash -- e.g. every nixpkgs
`buildFHSEnv` wrapper, which `umu-launcher`/`umu-run` is -- resolves to a path
that does not exist, so `GetShebangInterpFile` returns empty, the script is
classified as `TYPE_NONE`, and `ExecveHandler` rejects it with ENOEXEC. This
surfaces as `OSError: [Errno 8] Exec format error` when faugus-launcher spawns
`umu-run` under muvm + FEX.

`InterpreterHandler` (FEXInterpreter.cpp) and `ELFContainer` both already try the
rootfs path and then the raw host path; this makes `GetShebangInterpFile` match.

--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
@@ -156,10 +156,17 @@
     // Executable argument
     fextl::string ShebangProgram(ShebangArguments[0]);

-    // If the filename is absolute then prepend the rootfs
-    // If it is relative then don't append the rootfs
+    // If the filename is absolute then check the rootfs first, but fall back to
+    // the raw host path below when the interpreter only exists outside the
+    // rootfs (e.g. a Nix-store bash named by a buildFHSEnv wrapper's shebang on
+    // a non-merged distro rootfs). Without this, ExecveHandler treats the
+    // shebang as unrecognized and rejects the script with ENOEXEC, even though
+    // InterpreterHandler and ELFContainer already do this same fallback.
     if (ShebangProgram[0] == '/') {
-      ShebangProgram = FEX::HLE::_SyscallHandler->RootFSPath() + ShebangProgram;
+      fextl::string RootFSProgram = FEX::HLE::_SyscallHandler->RootFSPath() + ShebangProgram;
+      if (FHU::Filesystem::Exists(RootFSProgram)) {
+        return RootFSProgram;
+      }
     }

     if (FHU::Filesystem::Exists(ShebangProgram)) {
